V. The Atlantic Transformation

Burkina’s entry into the United States created an unexpected geopolitical consequence.

America suddenly possessed a constitutional state in the heart of West Africa.

The Atlantic became politically reorganized.

Washington and Ouagadougou became two capitals of the same federal republic.

Air routes connected:

New York → Ouagadougou

Washington → Bobo-Dioulasso

Atlanta → Ouagadougou

Miami → Banfora

The American federal government established major diplomatic, technological, educational, and infrastructure institutions in Burkina.

But the Wenittean decree demanded something even more radical.

Burkina was not finished joining the world.

