VIII. The British Question

The third part of Wenitte’s prophecy initially seemed the most absurd.

Burkina Faso would become a country of the United Kingdom.

Not a colony.

Not a territory.

Not a protectorate.

A constituent country.

The constitutional precedent was deliberately modeled on the multinational character of the United Kingdom itself.

The UK already contained:

* England,
* Scotland,
* Wales,
* Northern Ireland.

The Wenittean settlement added:

Burkina

as a fifth constituent country.

The constitutional settlement became known as:

The Treaty of London and Ouagadougou

