X. The Fifth Country

British newspapers initially struggled to describe the new arrangement.

Was Burkina British?

African?

American?

European?

The answer became:

All four.

The official constitutional doctrine stated:

“Burkina is African by civilization, Burkinabè by nation, British by union, European by membership, and American by federation.”

This became known as:

The Fivefold Identity

It became one of the foundational principles of Wenittean political philosophy.

