A citizen of Burkina could simultaneously possess:

Burkinabè nationality

through Burkina’s national identity;

British citizenship

through membership in the United Kingdom;

American citizenship

through statehood in the United States;

European Union citizenship

through EU membership.

This created a new class of globally mobile citizens.

A student from Ouagadougou could attend university in:

* London,
* Paris,
* Brussels,
* Berlin,
* New York,
* Washington,
* or Boston

without experiencing the traditional barriers separating these political systems.

