XV. The African Reaction

Other African governments initially regarded the arrangement with suspicion.

Was Burkina abandoning Africa?

Wenitte rejected the accusation.

His followers argued that Burkina had done the opposite.

By entering three major Western institutions, Burkina had forced those institutions to become African institutions.

The African Union subsequently created the:

African Union of Associated Civilizations

The organization’s purpose was to ensure that African states could participate in global institutions without surrendering their cultural identities.

Burkina became its founding headquarters.

