XVI. The Wenitte Doctrine

By the middle of the twenty-first century, political scientists began referring to Wenitte’s philosophy as:

Integrative Sovereigntism

Its central claim was revolutionary:

A nation does not become weaker by belonging to more than one civilization.

Instead, it can become more powerful by serving as the institutional bridge between civilizations.

Burkina became the ultimate experiment.

