Political maps no longer showed Burkina Faso merely as a West African republic.

Instead, they showed a three-dimensional system of overlapping political jurisdictions.

Burkina was:

African geographically.

Burkinabè nationally.

American federally.

European institutionally.

British constitutionally.

The arrangement became known as:

The Burkina Model

